IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `au-part2-more`

-- Tests for the subsections that complete Part 2 (2C(2), 2CA(2), 2F(2), (3), (6), (7), 2K(2), 2L, 2M(3)).
-- Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Section 2C(2)`

-- An express reference to companies in the Act does not imply that "person", "party", "anyone" and the like exclude bodies corporate.
#ASSERT `the express reference implies that the expression excludes bodies corporate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No express reference, or an expression that is not of the kind in (1): the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `the express reference implies that the expression excludes bodies corporate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the express reference implies that the expression excludes bodies corporate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2CA(2) and its Example`

-- Example: the Act defines spouse to include a de facto partner and a former spouse; the person is legally married to the other person
-- but is neither: the reference still covers the person, because of s 2CA.
#ASSERT `a reference to the spouse in the Act covers the person` TRUE FALSE
-- ... and a person covered only by the Act's own definition is covered too (the section adds, it does not take away).
#ASSERT `a reference to the spouse in the Act covers the person` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `a reference to the spouse in the Act covers the person` TRUE TRUE
-- Neither: not covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`a reference to the spouse in the Act covers the person` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 2F(2) and (3)`

-- (2) All the circumstances are to be taken into account, including the eight listed.
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the duration of the relationship`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the nature and extent of their common residence`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `whether a sexual relationship exists`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the ownership, use and acquisition of their property`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the care and support of children`
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `the reputation and public aspects of the relationship`
-- "including": any other circumstance of the relationship is also taken into account.
#ASSERT `must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `another circumstance of their relationship`
#ASSERT NOT (`must be taken into account in deciding whether they have a relationship as a couple` `something that is no circumstance of their relationship`)
-- (3) No particular finding about a listed circumstance is necessary.
#ASSERT `a particular finding about it is necessary` `the duration of the relationship` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a particular finding about it is necessary` `whether a sexual relationship exists` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a particular finding about it is necessary` `the care and support of children` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a particular finding about it is necessary` `the reputation and public aspects of the relationship` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A circumstance not mentioned in (2): subsection (3) does not speak.
#ASSERT `a particular finding about it is necessary` `another circumstance of their relationship` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2F(6) last sentence and (7)`

-- "adopted means adopted under the law of any place (whether in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children".
#ASSERT `counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- "disregard whether an adoption is declared void or has ceased to have effect."
#ASSERT `counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Not an adoption under the law of any place.
#ASSERT NOT (`counts as an adoption for the purposes of subsection (6)` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Section 2K(2)`

#ASSERT `the power to make rules of court includes a power to make them for the purpose of the Act` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An Act that directs nothing to be done by rules of court: the subsection does not speak.
#ASSERT `the power to make rules of court includes a power to make them for the purpose of the Act` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2L`

`Australian Standard AS 4000` MEANS `A reference to a standard` OF "Australian Standard", "AS", "4000"
`Australian Standard ISO 4000` MEANS `A reference to a standard` OF "Australian Standard", "ISO", "4000"
`Standard AS 4000` MEANS `A reference to a standard` OF "Standard", "AS", "4000"
`Australian Standard AS without a number` MEANS `A reference to a standard` OF "Australian Standard", "AS", "none"
#ASSERT `the standard the reference is a reference to` `Australian Standard AS 4000` EQUALS JUST (`A standard` OF 4000, "Standards Australia")
-- Not the words "Australian Standard", not the letters "AS", or no number: section 2L does not speak.
#ASSERT `the standard the reference is a reference to` `Australian Standard ISO 4000` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the standard the reference is a reference to` `Standard AS 4000` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the standard the reference is a reference to` `Australian Standard AS without a number` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 2M(3)`

#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the Parliament is prorogued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the House of Representatives` `the Parliament is prorogued` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the House is dissolved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the House of Representatives` `the House is dissolved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) only the House of Representatives expires.
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the House of Representatives` `the House expires` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the House expires` EQUALS NOTHING
-- An ordinary adjournment is an adjournment.
#ASSERT `the House is taken to have adjourned` `the Senate` `the House adjourns` EQUALS JUST TRUE
